NAME
       openpty - open a pseudo-terminal pair

SYNOPSIS
       #include <pty.h>

       int openpty(int *master, int *slave, char *name,
                   const struct termios *tio, const struct winsize *ws);

DESCRIPTION
       Creates a terminal pair. What is written to the master appears
       as input on the slave, and what a program writes to the slave
       comes back on the master.

       This is what lets sshd give a remote login a real terminal, and
       what wterm uses to run a shell inside a framebuffer window: the
       shell believes it is talking to a terminal, and line editing and
       job control work normally.

RETURN VALUE
       0 on success, -1 with errno set.

ERRORS
       ENOENT   no pseudo-terminal is free

SEE ALSO
       vt(2), sshd(1), wterm(1), termios(3)
